 "notes": "DEER = 2025 season, PER HUNT/ZONE, from CDFW '2025 California Deer Harvest Statistics' Table 1 (https://nrm.dfg.ca.gov/FileHandler.ashx?DocumentID=245246&inline, linked from https://wildlife.ca.gov/Hunting/Deer; data as of April 13, 2026; excludes Section 554 landowner and PLM harvest). harvest = CDFW 'Total Estimated' deer kill (reported kill adjusted for the non-reporting rate); successPct = CDFW 'Percent Hunter Success' = total estimated kill / tags issued. hunters = null (CDFW prints tag quota, not tags issued or hunters afield). B-zone, C-zone and D3-5 tags are good in a group of zones: harvest is per zone but CDFW's success % is for the whole group (said in the label). Draw hunt 'C' (C1-C4 tag) has its own row with the group figure and harvest null. Statewide archery-only (AO) and fundraising (Gold Opp, Open Zone) rows are left out. Units use CDFW BIOS layer spellings (X3a, not X3A). ELK / PRONGHORN / BIGHORN SHEEP = 2025 season, PER HUNT, from the '2025 Hunter Success (%)' column of the 2026 California Big Game Digest hunt tables (https://nrm.dfg.ca.gov/FileHandler.ashx?DocumentID=200602&inline, elk pp.48-52, pronghorn pp.58-59, bighorn p.61). Only the percent is published (hunters and harvest null). Hunts printed '-' are left out. Pronghorn hunt 790 (Zone 4 Lassen apprentice) is left out: the Digest prints 80% in one table and 100% in another. Newer per-hunt elk / pronghorn harvest PDFs with counts stop at 2022 (elk) and 2023 (pronghorn) on wildlife.ca.gov, so they were not used.",
